# Deploy

GitHub is version control only. Never GitHub Pages, `actions/deploy-pages`, or
`withastro/action`. Never treat a merge to `main` or a green GitHub check as
published.

**Published** = a visitor can see the change at https://rtikhonov.com

## Live tree (read this first)

Production is Cloudflare Worker `rtikhonov`, custom domains `rtikhonov.com` and
`www.rtikhonov.com`.

Source of truth:

- Folder: `rtikhonov.com/` (must contain `wrangler.jsonc`)
- Git line: `cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting` and PRs based on it
- Command: `cd rtikhonov.com && npm run deploy` (docs check + build + Wrangler)

The repo-root Astro app on `main` (root `package.json`, no `wrangler.jsonc`) is
**not** the live site. If this checkout lacks `rtikhonov.com/wrangler.jsonc`:

```bash
git fetch origin cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting
git checkout -b cursor/<change>-433e origin/cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting
```

Edit files under `rtikhonov.com/src/`. Do not implement the live change on the
root `main` site.

## Auth (before any ship)

Cloud / CI agents need env `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`
if Wrangler asks). Desktop can use `npx wrangler login`.

```bash
cd rtikhonov.com && npx wrangler whoami
```

If this fails: stop. Ask the owner to add `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` to the Cursor
Cloud environment secrets (Workers Scripts Edit). Do not merge and say it is
live. Do not run `wrangler login` and wait on a localhost OAuth callback.

## Ship

```bash
# Desktop nvm (skip if node >= 22.12 is already on PATH):
export PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.18.0/bin:$PATH"
cd rtikhonov.com && npm run deploy
```

`npm run deploy` already runs `check:docs` and `astro build`. If `git status`
is dirty with undocumented user-facing work, update docs/changelog first.

Expect ~30–60s. Need network. Then **verify the live URL** (cache-bust):

```bash
curl -sS -H "Cache-Control: no-cache" "https://rtikhonov.com/?t=$(date +%s)" | rg -n "your-new-string"
```

Report Wrangler Version ID plus https://rtikhonov.com (and only call it
published if the curl/page shows the change).

## Do not

- TodoWrite for a clean-tree deploy
- `git diff main...HEAD` unless the deploy failed
- Re-run `check:docs` / `astro build` before `npm run deploy` when the tree is clean
- Commit or push unless asked (except when a PR is already the agreed path)
- Hard-require `/Users/rtikhonov/Desktop/...` — that is the owner laptop only.
  In this repo use `rtikhonov.com/` from the repository root.
